{
  "intro": [
    {
      "text": "A mysterious power on Roshar: a person who seeks out the Nightwatcher receives a boon, and always a curse with it.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" }]
    }
  ],
  "description": [
    {
      "text": "The Old Magic gives boons and curses through the Nightwatcher: whatever the boon, a curse comes with it.",
      "revealedIn": [{ "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" }]
    },
    {
      "text": "A person gains a single unique ability from the Old Magic, and a unique curse along with it.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "prologue" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Khriss's Ars Arcanum calls it a cousin to Voidbinding.",
      "revealedIn": [
        {
          "all": [
            { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
            { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "prologue" }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "history": [],
  "mechanics": [
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Boons",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" },
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-12" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Anyone may seek one boon. The exact phrasing of the request makes no difference: the Nightwatcher gives the boon she feels the person deserves.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "She says she can grant almost anything, even spheres, gemstones, Shards, or a Blade that bleeds darkness, but she struggles with nebulous requests about human emotion.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" }]
        },
        {
          "text": "A person's boon and curse stay with them for life, even if they leave Roshar.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "111" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In very rare cases, Cultivation gives a boon and curse herself, in a far more calculated manner.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" },
                { "book": "rhythm-of-war", "chapter": "i-12" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": [
        {
          "text": "Curses",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" }
              ]
            },
            { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "epilogue" }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "No careful phrasing avoids the curse, and no one can predict which curse will come.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Many have searched for centuries for a cure for their curse, without success.",
          "revealedIn": [
            {
              "all": [
                { "book": "way-of-kings", "chapter": "i-7" },
                { "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "114" }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Dalinar is the only person known to have been rid of a curse, and that was part of the curse itself: he would one day have to face the loss of Evi.",
          "revealedIn": [{ "book": "oathbringer", "chapter": "epilogue" }]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
